## Why This Is Asked
This question assesses the ability to design a runtime-extensible plugin architecture for critical control logic. It tests understanding of extensibility patterns, safety considerations, and observability requirements under high-load production environments similar to those at Netflix, Tesla, or Oracle.

## Key Concepts
- **Strategy Pattern**: Encapsulates each evaluation algorithm (Boolean, Percentage, UserSegment) behind a common interface
- **Registry/Plugin Loader**: Maintains a map of evaluator names to implementations, enabling runtime registration without redeployment
- **Hot-Reloadable Modules**: Allows new evaluators to be added or updated without restarting the service
- **Per-Flag Isolation**: Each flag has dedicated configuration and metrics to prevent cascade failures
- **Observability**: Built-in logging, metrics, and audit trails for every flag evaluation

## Code Example
```typescript
interface FlagEvaluationContext {
  userId?: string;
  attributes?: Record<string, any>;
  [key: string]: any;
}

interface FlagConfig {
  key: string;
  strategy: string;
  parameters?: Record<string, any>;
  enabled?: boolean;
}

interface IFlagEvaluator {
  name: string;
  evaluate(config: FlagConfig, context: FlagEvaluationContext): boolean;
}

class FlagRegistry {
  private evaluators = new Map<string, IFlagEvaluator>();
  private cache = new Map<string, IFlagEvaluator>();

  register(evaluator: IFlagEvaluator): void {
    this.evaluators.set(evaluator.name, evaluator);
    this.cache.delete(evaluator.name);
  }

  get(name: string): IFlagEvaluator | undefined {
    if (!this.cache.has(name)) {
      this.cache.set(name, this.evaluators.get(name));
    }
    return this.cache.get(name);
  }

  evaluate(config: FlagConfig, ctx: FlagEvaluationContext): boolean {
    const evaluator = this.get(config.strategy);
    if (!evaluator) throw new Error(`Unknown strategy: ${config.strategy}`);
    return evaluator.evaluate(config, ctx);
  }
}

// Built-in evaluators
const BooleanEvaluator: IFlagEvaluator = {
  name: 'Boolean',
  evaluate: (config) => config.parameters?.value === true,
};

const PercentageEvaluator: IFlagEvaluator = {
  name: 'Percentage',
  evaluate: (config, ctx) => {
    const percentage = config.parameters?.percentage ?? 0;
    const hash = this.hash(ctx.userId ?? Math.random().toString());
    return (hash % 100) < percentage;
  },
  hash: (str: string) => str.split('').reduce((a, b) => ((a << 5) - a) + b.charCodeAt(0), 0),
};

// Usage
const registry = new FlagRegistry();
registry.register(BooleanEvaluator);
registry.register(PercentageEvaluator);

const result = registry.evaluate(
  { key: 'new-feature', strategy: 'Percentage', parameters: { percentage: 25 } },
  { userId: 'user-123' }
);
```

## Why This Is Asked
